Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Istio Sidecar Not Injected
If you notice pods don't have 2/2 containers:

# Check if namespace has injection label
kubectl get namespace resilient-apps --show-labels

# If missing, add the label
kubectl label namespace resilient-apps istio-injection=enabled

# Restart deployments to inject sidecars
kubectl rollout restart deployment/frontend -n resilient-apps
kubectl rollout restart deployment/backend -n resilient-apps
Issue 2: Circuit Breaker Not Triggering
If circuit breaker doesn't seem to work:

# Check DestinationRule configuration
kubectl describe destinationrule backend-circuit-breaker -n resilient-apps

# Verify outlier detection settings
kubectl get destinationrule backend-circuit-breaker -n resilient-apps -o yaml
Issue 3: Load Balancing Not Working
If load balancing seems ineffective:

# Check service endpoints
kubectl get endpoints -n resilient-apps

# Verify DestinationRule load balancer settings
kubectl get destinationrule backend-load-balancing -n resilient-apps -o yaml
Issue 4: Monitoring Dashboards Not Accessible
If dashboards are not accessible:

# Check if monitoring components are running
kubectl get pods -n istio-system

# Restart port forwarding
pkill -f "kubectl port-forward"
kubectl port-forward -n istio-system svc/kiali 20001:20001 &
kubectl port-forward -n istio-system svc/grafana 3000:3000 &
Best Practices Summary
Retry Configuration Best Practices
Set reasonable retry limits: Too many retries can overwhelm failing services
Use exponential backoff: Implement progressive delays between retries
Retry on specific conditions: Only retry on transient failures (5xx, timeouts)
Set per-try timeouts: Prevent individual retries from taking too long
Circuit Breaker Best Practices
Configure appropriate thresholds: Balance between sensitivity and stability
Set reasonable ejection times: Allow sufficient time for services to recover
Monitor ejection percentages: Ensure minimum healthy instances remain
Use health checks: Implement proper health endpoints for accurate detection
Load Balancing Best Practices
Choose appropriate algorithms: LEAST_CONN for varying request durations, ROUND_ROBIN for uniform requests
Configure connection limits: Prevent resource exhaustion
Implement health checks: Ensure traffic only goes to healthy instances
Use subset routing: Implement canary deployments and A/B testing
